Z||000000||watts||12-17-2001||01:14 AM||||I'm pretty damn sure this has been touched on before, but...  I can't find it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>When you turn the key over to 'start', the temp gauge 'whacks' over to the far right.  I seem to remember a thread talking about this, and that there's a wire to cut somewhere to make it stop.<P>It hits so hard that the needle is almost falling off now!  And it keeps reading lower and lower as the needle rotates on the pin.<P>Ideas?  Memories?<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||heavyhorse||12-17-2001||08:48 AM||||it's been some time, but hwen this happened to me i ended up replacing the temp/fuel guage assembly.  i was also having, what appeared to be an out of calibration reading.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||12-17-2001||09:00 AM||||Instructions on how to correct the pegging temp gauge problem can be found on the Michigan Fiero Club website at <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A> <P>Read the instructions carefully.  They have 2 versions of these instructions posted, and if I remember correctly one of the versions has the wrong wire shown in the picture but it is discussed correctly in the text instructions.<P>I have done this mod on both of my 87 GT's and it works great.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||watts||12-17-2001||10:29 AM||||Perfect!  That's it!  I knew I'd heard it somewhere...<P>Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
